<%# 1. Reset the "new label" trigger so the user can create another.

    UPDATE, NOT REPLACE — the same bug the add-a-card trigger had (see
    cards/create.turbo_stream.erb). `new_label_row` IS a turbo-frame
    (cards/show.html.erb wraps the trigger in one, and labels/cancel_new.html.erb
    puts it back), so `replace` swapped the frame itself out for a bare <a>.
    The link carries data-turbo-frame="new_label_row", so once the frame was gone
    the next "Create a new label" click had no frame to target and fell back to a
    full-page visit to /boards/:id/labels/new — a template that renders nothing
    but cards/_label_form, itself only a turbo_frame_tag. Card modal and board
    gone, page reduced to a lone label form.

    Rendering the shared trigger partial rather than an inlined copy of the link:
    labels/cancel_new.html.erb already used it, and this copy had drifted (it was
    missing the focus-visible ring the partial carries). %>
<% card = @card %>
<%= turbo_stream.update "new_label_row" do %>
  <%= render "cards/new_label_trigger", card: card %>
<% end %>

<%# 2. Append the freshly-created label row into the picker list.
       The list container is the "space-y-1 max-h-64 overflow-y-auto" div —
       we need a stable id on it. (Add the id in show.html.erb — see note.) %>
<%= turbo_stream.append "labels_list_#{@board.id}" do %>
  <%= render "cards/label_row", card: card, label: @label %>
<% end %>
